scout] to the giant's fort to the south east but they have not returned, and we have need of someone to track them down.'\nYou say, 'scout'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Give Us Your Tired'.\nTobart Dirkins says, 'The scout was last seen heading south, I believe they wanted to check the guard towers first before heading to the giant's fort. You may want to start your search there.'\n\n---\n\n_Tobart is worried about the scout that was sent to the giant's fort to the southeast. He fears the worst and needs someone to look into what happened while he tends to the survivors. He can't fetch the scout and look after everyone's safety and he has asked you to look into it._\n_Tobart mentioned that the count may have gone south and went to the guard huts along the river._\n1\\. Find Travit 0/1 (The Great Divide)\nTravit Conwill is inside one of the small towers (east tower) just a few steps south of Tobart along the frozen river. Enter to tower for quest update.\nYour task, 'Give Us Your Tired' has been updated.\n2\\. Return to Tobart and explain to him what you found 0/1 (The Great Divide)\nYou say, 'Hail, Tobart Dirkins'\nYou have been given: Tobart's Torch\nYour task 'Give Us Your Tired' has been updated.\nTobart Dirkins says, 'That news is... rather unsettling. Well, we know that if he stays out there like that, he will only return as a bigger problem as one of those... things. Please take this and dispose of his body. In the meantime, I will write up a new missive for the giants.\nYou receive a Tobart's Torch [item=138528] on your cursor.\n3\\. Return to Travit's body with Tobart's Torch 0/1 (The Great Divide)\nUpon getting within close proximity to Travit, he will attack you.\nTravit jumps up and attacks you!\nTravit Conwil says, 'Leeeeave... meeeee... aloooooone...'\n4\\. Dispose of Travit's body using Tobart's Torch 0/1 (The Great Divide)\nEngage with Travit Conwill.\nTravit Conwil's corpse cries out, 'Forgive me... master...'\nTravit Conwil has been slain!\nYour task 'Give Us Your Tired' has been updated.\nYour task 'Give Us Your Tired' has been updated.\n5\\. Return the torch to Tobart 0/1 (The Great Divide)e\nHand the torch back to Tobart.\nYou have been given: Travit's Missive [item=138529] (appears on cursor)\nYour task 'Give Us Your Tired' has been updated.\nTorbart Dirkins says, 'Well, as if things couldn't get any worse for us here, now I have to put up guards to watch out for our own. Every one of us that falls will become consumed by the ice, and then become one of them. They no longer have any semblance of free will. They become animals, feral and inhumane. Hopefully the giants will be a bit more [ **welcoming**] than the rest of this wasteland.'\nYou say, **welcoming**.\nTobart Dirkins says, 'Well, I guess you won't be needing that torch anymore. Thank you for your help with Travit, adventurer. He will be missed. You seem more than capable of handling yourself. Should the giants be less than welcoming, handle them too. Please, protect us from these harsh elements.\n6\\. Deliver the missive to the giants 0/1 (The Great Divide)e\nHand the _Travit's Missive_ over to Bekerak Coldbones.\nYour task, 'Give us Your Tired' has been updated.\nBekerak Coldbones says, 'This is unfortunate, tiny one. My people are starving and have nothing more to give. As you can see, the undead have also taken over the Great Divide. From what I understand, we aren't the only ones in this place and have been sundered by the ice. Not only have my people been affected, but so have the tizmak and the Coldain. The Coldain from Thurgadin have come to a place that is just as plagued as the place that they hail from. If we have any change in our situation, we will be able to welcome them, as we need allies in these dark times. However, until then, I have my own people to worry about and we cannot assist them. Please send my apologies.'\n7\\. Return to Tobart and let him know what Bekerak said 0/1 (The Great Divide)\nYou say, 'Hail, Tobart Dirkins'\nYour task 'Give Us Your Tired' has been updated.\nWhat happened to Travit was tragic, but it is a sullen reminder even the strongest needs to be careful in this cursed land.\nTobart Dirkins says, 'Please tell me that you have good [ **news**].'\nYou say, ' **News**.'\nTobart Dirkins says, 'This is... less than fortunate for our situation. Though we are hearty folks, I'm not sure how much longer we can hold out. Hopefully some bright tidings are in our future soon. I will try to send more people to find the cave the other survivors reconnoitered. If you have any booze, while it pains me to say, you may want to keep a distance from here. You will cause a scene with Horasug and everyone here is already on edge.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n106platinum 2 gold 5 silver\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
